      "writtenOn": "2013-11-07T00:28:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "base64url_percent_encode() above does a validation check on the input text. Thank you for calling attention to the fact an equivalent check was omitted from the decode operation.  The API should be symmetric providing both encode and decode. The idea behind these \"helper\" functions is to utilize the context in which the operation is occurring. In this case it\u0027s not just any text being encoded/decoded, rather it\u0027s base64 that has to meet certain specific criteria. Also the helper functions frees the user of the module from having to research the specific escape mechanism as defined in the RFC and locate the appropriate function in another unrelated Python module.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAATn//dmk\u003d",
      "revId": "09e87618400333c7fd3abc0a80af0801f8d794a6",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
